  "token_note": "(?-i:...) re-disables the global IGNORECASE inside name captures: Ghana operators print counterparties in upper case, and that is what bounds the lazy quantifier. Mixed-case names are therefore out of coverage for v1 and are counted as a tag in the evaluation. NDELIM*_HARD's lowercase-word terminator is wrapped in (?-i:...) on purpose: the whole pattern runs case-insensitively, and an unprotected [a-z] lookahead would also fire before UPPERCASE words, truncating 'NADIR FURNITURE' to 'NADIR'.",
