    "do not reply to this message[^.]*\\.",
    "not you\\?[^.]{0,40}\\.",
    "thank you for using[^.]*\\.",
    "top up more at any agent[^.]*\\.",
    "visit any agent[^.]*\\.",
    "download the [a-z0-9 ]+app[^.]*\\."
  ],
  "boilerplate_note": "Operator boilerplate sentences. Left in place they poison field extraction ('Dial *170# to manage your wallet' reads as a USSD channel, 'Top up more at any agent' as an agent cash-in). Templates are ^-anchored and unaffected, so this is stripped only for the per-field pass. Shared by normalize.py and the generated Kotlin."
